ace permanently.", "historical_evidence": "In previous incident ''Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host'' (INC-2026-1011), applying fail2ban and key-only auth resolved the breach with 0 unauthorized access.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement automated AWS Config / Cloud Custodian rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22", "Deploy Cloudflare / AWS WAF rate-limiting rule on authentication gateways", "Enforce FIDO2 / hardware MFA for all administrative and service accounts"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-1011", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.", "actions_taken": "Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "lessons_learned": "Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.", "analyst_feedback": ""}, {"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force