self-service consent halts ongoing tenant compromise.", "historical_evidence": "Historical memory from INC-2026-0815 confirmed that disabling user consent policy eliminated recurring spear-phishing vulnerability.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Enforce tenant-wide policy requiring administrator approval for third-party OAuth apps", "Implement conditional access policies blocking risky cloud logins", "Conduct regular automated OAuth application permission audits"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-0815", "title": "Executive Spear Phishing with OAuth Consent Grant", "type": "Phishing Attempt", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Illicit consent grant attack exploiting default user permission allowing non-admin users to authorize third-party OAuth apps.", "actions_taken": "Revoked OAuth token, deleted rogue Azure Enterprise App, terminated all active sessions for CFO, and removed hidden inbox forwarding rules.", "successful_resolution": "Revoked enterprise app consent, reset user credentials, and restricted tenant-wide user consent settings to verified publisher apps only.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce admin consent workflow for all third-party OAuth integrations across M365 tenant.", "analyst_feedback": "Illicit consent phishing is harder to detect than credential theft. Disabling user consent policy was the permanent fix."}, {"id": "INC-2026-1011", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "66%", "similarity_score": 0.66, "root_cause": "Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.", "actions_taken": "Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "lessons_learned": "Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.", "analyst_feedback": ""}, {"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "66%", "similarity_score": 0.66, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface."}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hindsight-local-INC-2026-1014');
