3. Verified bastion host session logs to confirm whether any login attempt succeeded.
4. Checked endpoint memory artifacts and PAM authentication daemon configuration.', 'Enforced perimeter firewall block on source subnet; rotated compromised credentials; disabled password authentication in sshd_config and enforced ed25519 key-only access.', 'SSH port restricted to internal management subnet (10.0.0.0/16); zero unauthorized ingress confirmed across 48-hour monitoring window.', 'AI triage correctly flagged the high-volume failure pattern and recommended immediate network isolation.', 'Enforce automated CI/CD security linting for SSH configurations and require mandatory MFA on all bastion jump hosts.', '2026-09-28T12:48:50Z', NULL, '{"incident_classification": "Credential Access - Automated Brute Force & Password Spraying (T1110)", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "Automated analysis of Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host targeting bastion-auth-gateway-02. Cross-referenced with Hindsight organizational memory.", "possible_root_cause": "Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.", "indicators": ["High-frequency failed authentication attempts from source IP 194.26.29.188", "Targeting service account ''root'' on bastion-auth-gateway-02", "Absence of progressive exponential backoff on auth endpoint"], "investigation_steps": ["Inspect SSH/auth logs on bastion-auth-gateway-02 to verify if any login attempts succeeded from 194.26.29.188", "Check GeoIP and Threat Intelligence reputation scores for source IP 194.26.29.188", "Verify if account ''root'' has multifactor authentication (MFA) actively enforced", "Audit PAM and firewall fail2ban delay configurations on the target host"], "recommended_response": ["Block malicious IP 194.26.29.188 at perimeter WAF / Security Group immediately", "Enforce SSH key-only authentication and disable password login on bastion-auth-gateway-02", "Restrict port 22/ingress to internal VPN CIDR (proven in INC-2026-1011)", "Force immediate credential rotation for account ''root''"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Historical incident INC-2026-1011 demonstrated that restricting ingress to VPN CIDR and disabling password auth eliminated brute-force surface permanently.", "historical_evidence": "In previous incident ''Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host'' (INC-2026-1011), applying fail2ban and key-only auth resolved the breach with 0 unauthorized access.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement automated AWS Config / Cloud Custodian rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22", "Deploy Cloudflare / AWS WAF rate-limiting rule on authentication gateways", "Enforce FIDO2 / hardware MFA for all administrative and service accounts"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-1011", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.", "actions_taken": "Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "lessons_learned": "Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.", "analyst_feedback": ""}, {"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0815", "title": "Executive Spear Phishing with OAuth Consent Grant", "type": "Phishing Attempt", "similarity": "68%", "similarity_score": 0.6799999999999999, "root_cause": "Illicit consent grant attack exploiting default user permission allowing non-admin users to authorize third-party OAuth apps.", "actions_taken": "Revoked OAuth token, deleted rogue Azure Enterprise App, terminated all active sessions for CFO, and removed hidden inbox forwarding rules.", "successful_resolution": "Revoked enterprise app consent, reset user credentials, and restricted tenant-wide user consent settings to verified publisher apps only.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce admin consent workflow for all third-party OAuth integrations across M365 tenant.", "analyst_feedback": "Illicit consent phishing is harder to detect than credential theft. Disabling user consent policy was the permanent fix."}], "memory_augmented": true}', NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1011', 'Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host', 'Brute-Force Attack', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'Over 38,000 failed SSH authentication attempts detected in 5 minutes targeting root and admin accounts.', '194.26.29.188', 'root', 'bastion-auth-gateway-02', 'sshd[14920]: Failed password for invalid user admin from 194.26.29.188 port 51230 ssh2
sshd[14921]: Failed password for root from 194.26.29.188 port 51232 ssh2
Max retries exceeded; connection dropped by rate limiter.', '2026-09-28T12:43:10Z', 'Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.', '1. Analyzed auth.log telemetry and identified 1,420 failed SSH attempts within a 4-minute window.
2. Traced source IP 192.168.1.105 via GeoIP intelligence to an unauthorized external proxy.
3. Verified bastion host session logs to confirm whether any login attempt succeeded.
4. Checked endpoint memory artifacts and PAM authentication daemon configuration.', 'Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.', 'Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.', 'AI triage correctly flagged the high-volume failure pattern and recommended immediate network isolation.', 'Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.', '2026-09-28T12:43:10Z', '2026-09-28T12:43:38Z', '{"incident_classification": "Credential Access - Automated Brute Force & Password Spraying (T1110)", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "Automated analysis of Distributed SSH Brute-Force on Bastion Host targeting bastion-auth-gateway-02. Cross-referenced with Hindsight organizational memory.", "possible_root_cause": "Directly exposed authentication port with legacy password authentication or unthrottled login endpoint.", "indicators": ["High-frequency failed authentication attempts from source IP 194.26.29.188", "Targeting service account ''root'' on bastion-auth-gateway-02", "Absence of progressive exponential backoff on auth endpoint"], "investigation_steps": ["Inspect SSH/auth logs on bastion-auth-gateway-02 to verify if any login attempts succeeded from 194.26.29.188", "Check GeoIP and Threat Intelligence reputation scores for source IP 194.26.29.188", "Verify if account ''root'' has multifactor authentication (MFA) actively enforced", "Audit PAM and firewall fail2ban delay configurations on the target host"], "recommended_response": ["Block malicious IP 194.26.29.188 at perimeter WAF / Security Group immediately", "Enforce SSH key-only authentication and disable password login on bastion-auth-gateway-02", "Restrict port 22/ingress to internal VPN CIDR (proven in INC-2026-0812)", "Force immediate credential rotation for account ''root''"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Historical incident INC-2026-0812 demonstrated that restricting ingress to VPN CIDR and disabling password auth eliminated brute-force surface permanently.", "historical_evidence": "In previous incident ''Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway'' (INC-2026-0812), applying fail2ban and key-only auth resolved the breach with 0 unauthorized access.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement automated AWS Config / Cloud Custodian rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22", "Deploy Cloudflare / AWS WAF rate-limiting rule on authentication gateways", "Enforce FIDO2 / hardware MFA for all administrative and service accounts"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0815", "title": "Executive Spear Phishing with OAuth Consent Grant", "type": "Phishing Attempt", "similarity": "68%", "similarity_score": 0.6799999999999999, "root_cause": "Illicit consent grant attack exploiting default user permission allowing non-admin users to authorize third-party OAuth apps.", "actions_taken": "Revoked OAuth token, deleted rogue Azure Enterprise App, terminated all active sessions for CFO, and removed hidden inbox forwarding rules.", "successful_resolution": "Revoked enterprise app consent, reset user credentials, and restricted tenant-wide user consent settings to verified publisher apps only.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce admin consent workflow for all third-party OAuth integrations across M365 tenant.", "analyst_feedback": "Illicit consent phishing is harder to detect than credential theft. Disabling user consent policy was the permanent fix."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0828", "title": "Suspicious Impossible Travel Login for Domain Admin", "type": "Suspicious Login", "similarity": "68%", "similarity_score": 0.6799999999999999, "root_cause": "Session token hijacking via Infostealer malware on the user''s unmanaged personal laptop used for remote work.", "actions_taken": "Revoked all active Okta and VPN sessions, reset user password, enforced hardware FIDO2 WebAuthn token requirement, quarantined remote laptop.", "successful_resolution": "Terminated rogue session, revoked cookies, upgraded admin account to hardware security key (FIDO2) which prevents token replay attacks.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce strict Device Trust / Zero Trust compliance so only corporate-managed laptops can connect to corporate VPN.", "analyst_feedback": "FIDO2 security key enforcement stopped session cookie replay vulnerability."}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hindsight-local-INC-2026-1011');
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1010', 'malware attack', 'Malware Detection', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'they was attacked to my maleware attack', '192.168.20.10', '@msrihari223', 'auth_gatway', NULL, '2026-09-28T12:39:33Z', 'Potential misconfiguration, credential exposure, or perimeter control gap.', '1. Ingested EDR process creation alerts indicating anomalous PowerShell execution with base64 payloads.
2. Extracted SHA-256 hash and submitted to VirusTotal / Sandbox analysis.
3. Queried network flow logs for command-and-control (C2) beaconing activity.
4. Scanned adjacent endpoints on the same VLAN for lateral propagation.', 'Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.', 'Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.', 'EDR telemetry integration allowed automated host containment within 90 seconds of alert trigger.', 'Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.', '2026-09-28T12:39:33Z', '2026-09-28T12:39:58Z', '{"incident_classification": "Threat Activity - Malware Detection", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "Automated analysis of malware attack targeting auth_gatway. Cross-referenced with Hindsight organizational memory.", "possible_root_cause": "Potential misconfiguration, credential exposure, or perimeter control gap.", "indicators": ["Unusual activity telemetry detected on auth_gatway", "Traffic originating from IP 192.168.20.10 involving user @msrihari223", "Alert thresholds exceeded in telemetry logs"], "investigation_steps": ["Isolate affected host or service auth_gatway from network segment", "Review authorization and access logs for user ''@msrihari223''", "Collect volatile memory and process execution telemetry for forensic analysis", "Cross-reference source indicators with threat intelligence databases"], "recommended_response": ["Quarantine impacted resource auth_gatway", "Invalidate active access credentials for @msrihari223", "Block source IP 192.168.20.10 at network perimeter"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Standard defense-in-depth isolation procedure.", "historical_evidence": "Matches organizational memory from INC-2026-1010", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement continuous posture monitoring and automated drift detection", "Strengthen endpoint telemetry and zero-trust authentication policies"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-1010", "title": "malware attack", "type": "Malware Detection", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Potential misconfiguration, credential exposure, or perimeter control gap.", "actions_taken": "Applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "lessons_learned": "Ensure port exposure audits run continuously.", "analyst_feedback": ""}, {"id": "INC-2026-0821", "title": "Cryptomining Binary Detected on Kubernetes Worker Node", "type": "Malware Detection", "similarity": "96%", "similarity_score": 0.9600000000000001, "root_cause": "Remote code execution vulnerability (CVE-2024-XXXX) in unpatched third-party image parser library in order-processing microservice.", "actions_taken": "Isolated infected pod, updated network policy to drop mining pool IPs, patched vulnerable container base image, redeployed with read-only root filesystem.", "successful_resolution": "Container rebuilt with patched dependencies, read-only rootfs enabled, mining IP CIDR blocked at egress gateway.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce container read-only root filesystems (`readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`) and vulnerability scanning in CI/CD pipeline.", "analyst_feedback": "Read-only filesystem prevented malware from writing persistence scripts."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "57%", "similarity_score": 0.58, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface."}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hindsight-local-INC-2026-1010');
