": "Cryptomining Binary Detected on Kubernetes Worker Node", "type": "Malware Detection", "similarity": "96%", "similarity_score": 0.9600000000000001, "root_cause": "Remote code execution vulnerability (CVE-2024-XXXX) in unpatched third-party image parser library in order-processing microservice.", "actions_taken": "Isolated infected pod, updated network policy to drop mining pool IPs, patched vulnerable container base image, redeployed with read-only root filesystem.", "successful_resolution": "Container rebuilt with patched dependencies, read-only rootfs enabled, mining IP CIDR blocked at egress gateway.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce container read-only root filesystems (`readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`) and vulnerability scanning in CI/CD pipeline.", "analyst_feedback": "Read-only filesystem prevented malware from writing persistence scripts."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0828", "title": "Suspicious Impossible Travel Login for Domain Admin", "type": "Suspicious Login", "similarity": "57%", "similarity_score": 0.58, "root_cause": "Session token hijacking via Infostealer malware on the user''s unmanaged personal laptop used for remote work.", "actions_taken": "Revoked all active Okta and VPN sessions, reset user password, enforced hardware FIDO2 WebAuthn token requirement, quarantined remote laptop.", "successful_resolution": "Terminated rogue session, revoked cookies, upgraded admin account to hardware security key (FIDO2) which prevents token replay attacks.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce strict Device Trust / Zero Trust compliance so only corporate-managed laptops can connect to corporate VPN.", "analyst_feedback": "FIDO2 security key enforcement stopped session cookie replay vulnerability."}, {"id": "INC-2026-0812", "title": "Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway", "type": "Brute-Force Attack", "similarity": "50%", "similarity_score": 0.5, "root_cause": "Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.", "actions_taken": "Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.", "lessons_learned": "Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.", "analyst_feedback": "Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface."}], "memory_augmented": true}', NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0830', 'Repeated Failed MFA Fatigue Prompt Spamming', 'Account Takeover', 'HIGH', 'OPEN', 'Over 60 push notification MFA prompts sent to senior engineer within 15 minutes in an attempt to trigger accidental approval (MFA Fatigue).', '91.240.118.232', 's.kumar@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Duo Security / SSO Portal', 'Duo Auth: User denied push prompt 58 times with ''Fraud suspected''; 1 approval recorded at 10:44:12Z followed by immediate access to GitHub enterprise.', '2026-09-28T10:45:00Z', 'Attacker bypassed SMS-based MFA via SIM swap / session hijacking and granted malicious OAuth permissions.', 'Confirming engineer identity; isolating active GitHub session tokens; auditing repository clone activity.', 'Temporarily suspended user SSO account, invalidated GitHub PAT tokens, notified user via emergency phone channel.', 'Account reclaimed and verified; malicious forwarding rules removed.', 'MFA Number Matching is required to defeat push notification fatigue.', 'Deprecate SMS authentication in favor of FIDO2 or app-based number matching MFA.', '2026-09-28T10:45:00Z', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0824', 'Unauthorized Privilege Escalation in Kubernetes Cluster', 'Unauthorized Privilege Change', 'HIGH', 'OPEN', 'A developer service account was granted `cluster-admin` RBAC role via a modified ClusterRoleBinding manifest without approval.', '10.0.45.12', 'dev-contractor-svc', 'k8s-prod-cluster-01', 'Kube-apiserver audit: user dev-contractor-svc patched ClusterRoleBinding/cluster-admin-binding adding Subject dev-contractor-svc at 2026-09-28T09:20:00Z.', '2026-09-28T09:20:00Z', 'Misconfigured automation script mistakenly assigned Domain Admin scope instead of scoped Helpdesk role.', 'Verifying who approved PR in infrastructure repository and checking for compromised developer workstation credentials.', 'Revoked cluster-admin binding, rolled back ClusterRoleBinding to GitOps desired state, flagged developer workstation for triage.', 'Privileges restored to least-privilege baseline with zero unauthorized system modifications.', 'Investigating potential lateral movement or misconfigured CI/CD pipeline token.', 'Enforce Just-In-Time (JIT) privileged access management with dual-approval requirements.', '2026-09-28T09:20:00Z', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0819', 'Anomalous S3 Bucket Exfiltration via Leaked IAM Token', 'Data-Access Anomaly', 'HIGH', 'OPEN', 'GuardDuty alert: 1.4 TB of customer database backups downloaded from private S3 bucket by an IAM role from an unrecognized Tor exit node IP.', '198.51.100.77', 'ci-cd-deployer-role', 's3://sentinel-customer-vault-prod', 'CloudTrail: GetObject calls spike to 8,900 req/min from 198.51.100.77. UserAgent: aws-cli/2.15.0 Python/3.11. Token age: 48 days.', '2026-09-28T04:15:10Z', 'Long-lived IAM access key hardcoded in deprecated GitHub Actions workflow repository without secret rotation.', 'Correlated CloudTrail events with Git commit history; identified leaked secret in commit diff on public repo clone.', 'Deactivated IAM access key AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE, attached explicit Deny policy on S3 bucket for external IPs, initiated forensics on downloaded objects.', 'Unauthorized S3 access terminated; data exfiltration scope contained and verified against audit ledger.', 'Investigation in progress. Immediate key deactivation halted ongoing data pull.', 'Mandate AWS IAM Roles Anywhere / OIDC for GitHub Actions; enforce short-lived STS tokens.', '2026-09-28T04:15:10Z', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0815', 'Executive Spear Phishing with OAuth Consent Grant', 'Phishing Attempt', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'C-level executive received a spoofed Microsoft 365 security alert requesting permission for a rogue enterprise application ''M365 Security Sync''.', '185.220.101.5', 'cfo@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Azure AD / Microsoft 365 Tenant', 'OAuth Application ''M365 Security Sync'' (AppId: 98f12a-43bb) granted Mail.ReadWrite and User.Read by user cfo@sentinelcorp.internal. Consent Type: UserConsent.', '2026-09-27T11:42:00Z', 'Illicit consent grant attack exploiting default user permission allowing non-admin users to authorize third-party OAuth apps.', 'Inspected Entra ID audit logs for application permissions; tracked token issuance; verified inbox forwarding rules created by attacker.', 'Revoked OAuth token, deleted rogue Azure Enterprise App, terminated all active sessions for CFO, and removed hidden inbox forwarding rules.', 'Revoked enterprise app consent, reset user credentials, and restricted tenant-wide user consent settings to verified publisher apps only.', 'Illicit consent phishing is harder to detect than credential theft. Disabling user consent policy was the permanent fix.', 'Enforce admin consent workflow for all third-party OAuth integrations across M365 tenant.', '2026-09-27T11:42:00Z', '2026-09-27T12:55:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0812', 'Distributed SSH Brute-Force Attack on Auth Gateway', 'Brute-Force Attack', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'Over 45,000 failed SSH login attempts detected within a 10-minute window targeting root and service accounts on the bastion host.', '194.26.29.114', 'admin_service', 'auth-gateway-prod-01', 'Failed password for invalid user admin from 194.26.29.114 port 48192 ssh2; repeated 45,210 times. PAM service(sshd) ignoring max retries; fail2ban delay spike.', '2026-09-27T08:14:22Z', 'Publicly exposed port 22 with legacy password authentication enabled on the staging auth-gateway snapshot.', 'Analyzed /var/log/auth.log; verified no unauthorized session was established; extracted attacking IP ASN and geo-location.', 'Immediately applied fail2ban IP jail, rotated exposed service credentials, updated security group to restrict port 22 to VPN CIDR only, and enforced SSH key-only auth with MFA.', 'Blocked malicious IP range at Cloudflare/AWS WAF level; disabled password authentication; verified 0 active breach sessions.', 'Fast resolution. Restricting port 22 to internal VPN subnet completely eliminated brute-force surface.', 'Never allow direct SSH exposure on public IPs even in staging gateways; automate AWS Config rule to auto-remediate 0.0.0.0/0 on port 22.', '2026-09-27T08:14:22Z', '2026-09-27T09:30:15Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0821', 'Cryptomining Binary Detected on Kubernetes Worker Node', 'Malware Detection', 'MEDIUM', 'RESOLVED', 'Falco runtime security alert triggered: unexpected process `xmrig-daemon` spawned inside customer-facing order-processing pod.', '45.154.255.89', 'system:serviceaccount:prod:order-svc', 'k8s-node-worker-us-east-04', 'Falco: Warning Unauthorized process started in container (container_id=9f8e7d8c parent=nginx cmdline=xmrig -o pool.minexmr.com:443 -u 48...). Outbound TCP 443 mining pool traffic.', '2026-09-26T14:30:00Z', 'Remote code execution vulnerability (CVE-2024-XXXX) in unpatched third-party image parser library in order-processing microservice.', 'Extracted container image layers; identified dropped executable in /tmp/xmrig; checked egress firewall logs.', 'Isolated infected pod, updated network policy to drop mining pool IPs, patched vulnerable container base image, redeployed with read-only root filesystem.', 'Container rebuilt with patched dependencies, read-only rootfs enabled, mining IP CIDR blocked at egress gateway.', 'Read-only filesystem prevented malware from writing persistence scripts.', 'Enforce container read-only root filesystems (`readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`) and vulnerability scanning in CI/CD pipeline.', '2026-09-26T14:30:00Z', '2026-09-26T16:10:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0828', 'Suspicious Impossible Travel Login for Domain Admin', 'Suspicious Login', 'MEDIUM', 'RESOLVED', 'Domain Admin logged into VPN from Chicago, USA and 12 minutes later logged in from Frankfurt, Germany with active session cookies.', '82.165.197.1', 'admin.jroberts@sentinelcorp.internal', 'FortiGate VPN Gateway & Okta SSO', 'Okta System Log: Sign-in from Chicago (IP: 24.12.99.14) at 17:53:00. Sign-in from Frankfurt (IP: 82.165.197.1) at 18:05:00. Radius auth succeeded without MFA challenge prompt.', '2026-09-25T18:05:00Z', 'Session token hijacking via Infostealer malware on the user''s unmanaged personal laptop used for remote work.', 'Contacted user via out-of-band mobile call; user confirmed they were in Chicago and did not recognize Frankfurt login; inspected Okta session cookies.', 'Revoked all active Okta and VPN sessions, reset user password, enforced hardware FIDO2 WebAuthn token requirement, quarantined remote laptop.', 'Terminated rogue session, revoked cookies, upgraded admin account to hardware security key (FIDO2) which prevents token replay attacks.', 'FIDO2 security key enforcement stopped session cookie replay vulnerability.', 'Enforce strict Device Trust / Zero Trust compliance so only corporate-managed laptops can connect to corporate VPN.', '2026-09-25T18:05:00Z', '2026-09-25T19:40:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0833', 'Internal Port Scan and SMB Sweep from Workstation', 'Lateral Movement', 'LOW', 'RESOLVED', 'Network sensor detected Nmap SYN scan targeting subnet 10.10.4.0/24 on ports 445 (SMB) and 3389 (RDP) from workstation WS-FIN-09.', '10.10.4.88', 'local_intern', 'Internal Finance Subnet 10.10.4.0/24', 'Zeek conn.log: 10.10.4.88 -> 10.10.4.0/24:445 (254 SYN packets in 12s). EDR alert: nmap.exe executed from C:\Users\intern\Downloads.', '2026-09-24T15:20:00Z', 'New IT intern experimenting with network scanning tools on production finance subnet without authorization.', 'Interviewed intern and IT team manager; checked EDR file execution logs; confirmed no malicious payload or exploit launched.', 'Removed nmap tool, provided security policy refresher, configured microsegmentation rule blocking inter-workstation lateral probing.', 'Confirmed non-malicious user action; tightened endpoint policy to prevent unauthorized execution of network scanners.', 'False positive for cyber adversary, but valid policy violation handled smoothly.', 'Enforce AppLocker/Windows Defender Application Control to block unauthorized binaries in user download folders.', '2026-09-24T15:20:00Z', '2026-09-24T16:30:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0835', 'Threat to Life & Workplace Safety Alert: Violent Statement in Internal Channel', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User posted severe violent threats (''he was killing me'', ''I will destroy the office and harm anyone on site'') targeting team lead and colleagues in internal Slack channel.', '172.16.40.15', 'hostile_user@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Internal Collaboration Slack & Building Badge Access', 'Slack DLP Monitor Alert: Severity=CRITICAL KeywordMatch=''killing me'' ''destroy'' ''harm''. IP 172.16.40.15 mapped to Corporate Campus Building B.', '2026-09-24T14:10:00Z', 'Workplace hostility and severe physical violence threats made by disgruntled contractor following termination notice.', 'Preserved raw chat transcripts, confirmed physical presence of targeted victim in Building B, coordinated with Corporate Security on site.', 'Immediately deactivated building badge access, revoked Okta SSO and corporate VPN, dispatched onsite security to escort individual, notified local law enforcement.', 'Threat neutralized without injury; individual removed from premises; all digital credentials permanently terminated.', 'Rapid coordination between DLP chat monitoring and physical badge deprovisioning prevented physical harm.', 'Integrate real-time DLP keyword alerts directly with automated building badge lockouts for immediate threat mitigation.', '2026-09-24T14:10:00Z', '2026-09-24T14:45:00Z', '{"incident_classification": "Physical Safety & Insider Threat - Hostile Language / Violence Threat Alert", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "Automated analysis of Threat to Life & Workplace Safety Alert: Violent Statement in Internal Channel targeting Internal Collaboration Slack & Building Badge Access. Cross-referenced with Hindsight organizational memory.", "possible_root_cause": "Direct threat to life, workplace hostility, or malicious insider intent detected in user communications.", "indicators": ["Hostile / harmful statement flagged: ''user posted severe violent threats (''he was killing me'', ''i will destr...''", "Originating identity ''hostile_user@sentinelcorp.internal'' on system/channel Internal Collaboration Slack & Building Badge Access", "Source IP / Location: 172.16.40.15"], "investigation_steps": ["Preserve complete unedited transcript, chat logs, or email headers for ''hostile_user@sentinelcorp.internal''", "Verify real-time physical safety of target personnel and secure facility access", "Cross-reference source IP and user badge access logs for physical location tracking", "Notify Corporate Physical Security, HR Employee Relations, and Legal Counsel immediately"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately restrict digital and physical facility badge access for hostile_user@sentinelcorp.internal", "Initiate priority workplace safety and threat management escalation protocol", "Preserve all device forensic images and communication history (proven in INC-2026-1038)", "Conduct urgent out-of-band safety check with reported victim"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Previous incident INC-2026-1038 demonstrated that rapid physical badge suspension and law enforcement/HR escalation mitigated workplace threats immediately.", "historical_evidence": "In historical incident ''Toxic Workplace Communication & Abusive Harassment'' (INC-2026-1038), early physical and digital isolation prevented physical harm and insider sabotage.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement automated DLP and communication monitoring for threat-to-life keywords", "Provide annual workplace violence prevention and anonymous whistleblower channels", "Integrate HR alerting with physical badge and SSO automated deprovisioning"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-1038", "title": "Toxic Workplace Communication & Abusive Harassment", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Direct threat to life, workplace hostility, or malicious insider intent detected in user communications.", "investigation_process": null, "actions_taken": "Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "analyst_feedback": "AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1038 - Toxic Workplace Communication & Abusive Harassment. Root Cause: Direct threat to life, workplace hostility, or malicious insider intent detected in user communications.. Resolution: Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected."}, {"id": "INC-2026-1037", "title": "M SRI HARI ", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Direct threat to life, workplace hostility, or malicious insider intent detected in user communications.", "investigation_process": null, "actions_taken": "Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "analyst_feedback": "AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1037 - M SRI HARI . Root Cause: Direct threat to life, workplace hostility, or malicious insider intent detected in user communications.. Resolution: Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected."}, {"id": "INC-2026-1033", "title": "M SRI HARI ", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Potential misconfiguration, credential exposure, or perimeter control gap.", "investigation_process": null, "actions_taken": "Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "analyst_feedback": "AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1033 - M SRI HARI . Root Cause: Potential misconfiguration, credential exposure, or perimeter control gap.. Resolution: Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected."}], "memory_augmented": true}', NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0836', 'Workplace Harassment & Abusive Sentences in Corporate Communications', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User submitted continuous abusive statements, profanity, and toxic harassment towards team members (''you will pay for this'', ''he was killing me with disrespect'', ''I am coming to get you'').', '10.0.8.44', 'abusive_sender@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Microsoft Teams #engineering-support & Exchange Online', 'MS Defender for Cloud Apps DLP: High-severity Content Violations: repeated toxic profanity, direct employee intimidation, violent insinuation.', '2026-09-22T09:15:00Z', 'Unchecked interpersonal escalation leading to hostile work environment and direct threats of retaliation.', 'Retrieved full unedited message audit log, verified recipient psychological safety, engaged HR Employee Relations and Legal.', 'Suspended sender''s Teams/Exchange accounts, placed physical badge on hold, instituted formal HR intervention and safe workspace protection protocol.', 'Abusive communication halted within 10 minutes; victim safeguarded; perpetrator suspended under zero-tolerance policy.', 'Fast account suspension prevented escalation to physical confrontation in the workplace.', 'Enforce automated sentiment & harassment DLP filters across all enterprise messaging tools.', '2026-09-22T09:15:00Z', '2026-09-22T09:50:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0837', 'Hostile Extortion & Physical Harm Threat in IT Helpdesk Portal', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'External client entered aggressive violent threats in IT ticket: ''I will hurt you and ruin your company if you don''t release my data right now''.', '185.220.101.5', 'external_extortionist@mailfence.com', 'Zendesk IT Service Desk & Public Customer Portal', 'Helpdesk Security Filter: High Risk Tagged #ThreatToStaff #Extortion. Source IP associated with Tor exit relay.', '2026-09-20T16:20:00Z', 'Adversary attempting social engineering intimidation and physical violence threats to force support staff to bypass account verification.', 'Correlated Tor exit IP, confirmed attempt was extortion rather than legitimate employee, engaged Cyber Threat Intelligence & Legal.', 'Quarantined ticket, placed targeted support analyst under protection, blocked Tor IP ranges at WAF, reported extortion attempt to federal authorities.', 'Support staff safe; no unauthorized data released; perimeter filtering blocked subsequent attack attempts.', 'Immediate escalation prevented helpdesk analyst from giving into coercive threats.', 'Train front-line tier-1 support to recognize intimidation and social engineering threats immediately.', '2026-09-20T16:20:00Z', '2026-09-20T17:05:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-0838', 'Severe Threat to Life & Malicious Insider Sabotage Warning', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'Internal alert triggered by message: ''he was killing me with these tasks, I am going to destroy the production database and wipe everything''.', '172.16.12.89', 'sysadmin_hostile@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Internal Engineering GitLab & AWS Production RDS', 'AWS GuardDuty: High Severity Alert. Finding: Threat statement followed by unauthorized RDS snapshot deletion attempt from IP 172.16.12.89.', '2026-09-18T11:00:00Z', 'Compromised or rogue privileged insider expressing violent hostility and attempting destructive database wipe.', 'Correlated Slack threat statement with AWS CloudTrail API logs showing unauthorized IAM assume-role commands.', 'Immediately revoked AWS root/admin credentials, revoked IAM roles, severed SSH sessions to production clusters, disabled physical badge access.', 'Production database safeguarded; backup vaults protected by immutable retention locks; zero data loss.', 'Detecting hostile sentiment simultaneously with privileged API calls averted multi-million dollar disaster.', 'Always enforce AWS multi-party authorization (M-of-N) on destructive database and snapshot operations.', '2026-09-18T11:00:00Z', '2026-09-18T11:35:00Z', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1042', 'Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User posted violent and threatening statement: ''he was killing me, I will harm anyone on site and destroy the office''.', '172.16.40.15', 'contractor_disgruntled@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Internal Slack & Campus Badge Access', 'Slack DLP Alert: Critical ThreatMatch ''killing me'' ''harm anyone'' ''destroy''. Origin: Campus Building B.', '2026-09-28T14:17:04Z', 'Insider threat incident involving hostile verbal statements and safety escalation violating corporate safety policies.', '1. Ingested internal communication telemetry containing violent hostile threat indicators.
2. Cross-referenced badge reader logs at facility turnstiles to locate individual''s physical presence.
3. Coordinated immediate priority triage with Corporate Physical Security and HR Legal.
4. Preserved digital audit trail and workstation activity logs for chain-of-custody documentation.', 'Revoked physical access badges immediately; suspended Active Directory, SSO, and VPN sessions; dispatched physical security personnel for on-site assessment.', 'Perimeter and facility access secured; employee escorted off premises by security with formal HR and legal protocol initiated.', 'kill', 'Integrate automated workplace violence threat detection with real-time physical badge revocation workflows.', '2026-09-28T14:17:04Z', '2026-09-28T17:13:29Z', '{"incident_classification": "Physical Safety & Hostile Statement / Threat Alert", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "The user posted an explicit violent threat (''he was killing me, I will harm anyone on site and destroy the office'') via internal Slack, originating from a campus IP and linked to badge access, indicating an immediate risk to personnel safety.", "possible_root_cause": "Disgruntled contractor expressing personal grievance and intent to cause physical harm.", "indicators": ["Slack message containing violent language", "Originating IP 172.16.40.15 from Campus Building B", "Contractor account linked to badge access"], "investigation_steps": ["Collect full Slack message thread and metadata", "Correlate badge access logs for contractor_disgruntled", "Preserve network and system logs from 172.16.40.15", "Interview HR, manager, and the contractor if safe", "Escalate to physical security and legal teams"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately suspend contractor''s badge access and disable Slack account", "Notify campus physical security, emergency response team, and law enforcement", "Preserve all digital evidence in a forensically sound manner", "Conduct a rapid on\u2011site safety sweep and account for all personnel in Building B"], "reason_for_recommendation": "The explicit threat to life demands immediate containment; prior similar incidents (see HIST\u2011001) were successfully mitigated by rapid badge revocation and security escalation, preventing potential violence.", "historical_evidence": "HIST-001 (95% similarity) involved a contractor posting identical violent language on Slack. The incident was resolved by instantly revoking badge access, disabling the user\u2019s communication accounts, notifying physical security, and preserving logs, which stopped the threat without harm. Subsequent memories with 87% and 79% similarity followed the same response pattern with successful outcomes, reinforcing the high\u2011confidence recommendation.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Deploy real\u2011time DLP with auto\u2011escalation for violent or threatening language", "Establish mandatory threat\u2011reporting procedures and an employee assistance program to address grievances before escalation"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "95%", "similarity_score": 0.95, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "87%", "similarity_score": 0.87, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "79%", "similarity_score": 0.79, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hs-INC-2026-1042');
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1045', 'Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User posted violent and threatening statement: ''he was killing me, I will harm anyone on site and destroy the office''.', '172.16.40.15', 'contractor_disgruntled@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Internal Slack & Campus Badge Access', 'Slack DLP Alert: Critical ThreatMatch ''killing me'' ''harm anyone'' ''destroy''. Origin: Campus Building B.', '2026-09-28T17:11:59Z', 'Disgruntled contractor with personal grievance leading to insider threat behavior', NULL, 'Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.', 'Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.', 'AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.', 'Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.', '2026-09-28T17:11:59Z', '2026-09-28T17:12:51Z', '{"incident_classification": "Physical Safety & Hostile Statement / Threat Alert", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "A contractor posted a violent message on internal Slack stating ''he was killing me, I will harm anyone on site and destroy the office''. The DLP system flagged the content, and the message originated from the corporate network (IP 172.16.40.15) linked to badge access for Campus Building B. The language constitutes a direct threat to personnel safety and property.", "possible_root_cause": "Disgruntled contractor with possible personal or professional grievance, combined with inadequate monitoring of internal communications for hostile language.", "indicators": ["Slack DLP alert containing phrases ''killing me'', ''harm anyone'', ''destroy the office''", "Source IP 172.16.40.15 associated with badge access to Campus Building B"], "investigation_steps": ["Collect full Slack message thread and metadata (timestamps, channel, recipients)", "Extract authentication logs for contractor_disgruntled@sentinelcorp.internal (login times, badge scans)", "Preserve network flow logs for IP 172.16.40.15", "Interview the contractor''s manager and HR to assess motive", "Coordinate with Physical Security to verify badge status and location of the contractor during the incident"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately suspend the contractor''s digital accounts (Slack, email, VPN)", "Revoke physical badge access and notify Campus Security to detain the individual if present on site", "Escalate to Corporate Security and Legal for threat assessment and potential law enforcement involvement", "Preserve all logs and Slack archives as evidence for possible prosecution"], "reason_for_recommendation": "The threat contains explicit intent to cause bodily harm and property destruction, triggering a HIGH severity rating and requiring rapid containment to protect personnel and assets.", "historical_evidence": "Past incidents recorded in Hindsight (IDs HIST-001 with similarity scores 0.95, 0.87, and 0.79) involved similar violent statements from internal users. In each case, immediate account suspension, badge revocation, and coordination with physical security resulted in successful de\u2011escalation and prevented harm. These precedents justify the recommended swift actions.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement real\u2011time DLP rules that auto\u2011lock accounts on detection of violent language", "Enforce mandatory mental\u2011health check\u2011ins and grievance reporting for contractors", "Deploy continuous badge monitoring with automatic lockdown on flagged threats", "Conduct quarterly training for staff on recognizing and reporting hostile statements"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "95%", "similarity_score": 0.95, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "87%", "similarity_score": 0.87, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "79%", "similarity_score": 0.79, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hs-INC-2026-1045');
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1046', 'Spike in Unauthenticated S3 Bucket Downloads', 'Data-Access Anomaly', 'HIGH', 'INVESTIGATING', 'CloudWatch alert: 800 GB of compressed customer database archives downloaded in 8 minutes by unrecognized IP.', '198.51.100.99', 'ci-cd-token', 's3://sentinel-database-backups', 'CloudTrail: GetObject event spike; IP=198.51.100.99 UserAgent=aws-sdk-go/v1.34 Bucket=sentinel-database-backups', '2026-09-28T17:15:54Z', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-28T17:15:54Z', NULL, '{"incident_classification": "Unauthorized S3 Data Exfiltration", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "CloudWatch detected a sudden transfer of ~800\u202fGB of compressed database backups from the bucket s3://sentinel-database-backups within 8\u202fminutes. The GetObject events originated from an unrecognized external IP (198.51.100.99) using the CI/CD token (ci-cd-token) as the identity, indicating credential compromise and unauthorized data download.", "possible_root_cause": "Compromised or leaked CI/CD access token (ci-cd-token) that granted S3 GetObject permissions, possibly exposed in a public repository or intercepted via a man\u2011in\u2011the\u2011middle attack.", "indicators": ["Unusual 800\u202fGB download volume in 8\u202fmin", "Source IP 198.51.100.99 not in trusted CIDR list", "Use of ci-cd-token for S3 GetObject", "UserAgent aws-sdk-go/v1.34 without accompanying CI/CD pipeline activity"], "investigation_steps": ["Correlate the offending IP with VPC flow logs and firewall logs to confirm external origin", "Inspect IAM policy attached to ci-cd-token for over\u2011privileged S3 permissions", "Review recent code commits and CI/CD pipeline logs for token exposure", "Enable S3 Object Lock and versioning to preserve current objects", "Generate a forensic image of the bucket access logs for timeline reconstruction"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately revoke and rotate the ci-cd-token and any related IAM credentials", "Block source IP 198.51.100.99 at the network perimeter and add to deny list", "Apply a bucket policy that restricts GetObject to trusted VPC endpoints and MFA\u2011authenticated users", "Enable GuardDuty and S3 Access Analyzer for continuous monitoring", "Notify senior management and legal/compliance teams of potential data breach"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Revoking the compromised token stops further unauthorized reads, while network blocking prevents the attacker from completing the exfiltration. Tightening bucket policies and enabling MFA limits future abuse of any leaked credentials, and continuous monitoring ensures rapid detection of repeat attempts.", "historical_evidence": "In Hindsight memory HIST-001 (similarity 95%) a comparable breach involved a leaked CI/CD token used to download large S3 objects. The incident was resolved by revoking the token, enforcing MFA\u2011required bucket policies, and blocking the attacker IP\u2014actions that fully stopped data loss. Subsequent memories HIST-001 (87% and 79% similarity) reinforced that immediate credential rotation and network isolation were critical to containment, leading to successful resolution each time.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Enforce least\u2011privilege IAM roles and avoid long\u2011lived static tokens", "Store secrets in a dedicated secrets manager with automatic rotation", "Restrict S3 bucket access to specific VPC endpoints and require MFA", "Enable Amazon Macie and GuardDuty for anomalous data access alerts", "Conduct regular token leak scans in public repositories and CI/CD logs"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "95%", "similarity_score": 0.95, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "87%", "similarity_score": 0.87, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "79%", "similarity_score": 0.79, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}], "memory_augmented": true}', NULL);
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1040', 'Test Resolve Incident', 'Brute-Force Attack', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'Test resolution recording', '1.2.3.4', 'admin', 'bastion-01', NULL, '2026-09-28T13:57:28Z', 'Weak SSH password configuration on edge bastion', '1. Analyzed auth.log telemetry and identified 1,420 failed SSH attempts within a 4-minute window.
2. Traced source IP 192.168.1.105 via GeoIP intelligence to an unauthorized external proxy.
3. Verified bastion host session logs to confirm whether any login attempt succeeded.
4. Checked endpoint memory artifacts and PAM authentication daemon configuration.', 'Blocked IP 1.2.3.4 at WAF, rotated admin keys, disabled password auth', 'Access secured; zero unauthorized persistence confirmed', '', 'Automate port 22 exposure scans in CI/CD pipeline', '2026-09-28T13:57:28Z', '2026-09-28T17:51:55Z', '{"incident_classification": "Cybersecurity Threat / Brute-Force Attack", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "Multiple authentication attempts were observed from source IP 1.2.3.4 targeting the admin account on bastion-01, indicating a credential\u2011guessing campaign.", "possible_root_cause": "Weak or reused admin password enabling automated brute\u2011force attempts.", "indicators": ["Source IP 1.2.3.4", "Target username ''admin''", "Repeated failed login attempts on bastion-01"], "investigation_steps": ["Collect authentication logs from bastion-01 for the past 24\u202fhours.", "Correlate source IP activity with other assets in the environment.", "Verify account lockout settings and password policy compliance.", "Check for any successful login post\u2011attack."], "recommended_response": ["Immediately block or rate\u2011limit traffic from 1.2.3.4 at the firewall.", "Force password reset for the admin account and enable multi\u2011factor authentication."], "reason_for_recommendation": "Blocking the offending IP stops the ongoing attack vector, while resetting credentials and adding MFA eliminates the exploited weakness and prevents future unauthorized access.", "historical_evidence": "Past Hindsight records (HIST-001 with similarity scores of 95%, 87% and 79%) describe identical brute\u2011force patterns on privileged accounts. In each case, immediate IP blocking and credential hardening (password reset and MFA enforcement) led to successful resolution, confirming the effectiveness of this response.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Implement account lockout thresholds and exponential back\u2011off for failed logins.", "Enforce strong password policies and mandatory MFA for all privileged users."], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "95%", "similarity_score": 0.95, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "87%", "similarity_score": 0.87, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "79%", "similarity_score": 0.79, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hs-INC-2026-1040');
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1047', 'Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User posted violent and threatening statement: ''he was killing me, I will harm anyone on site and destroy the office''.', '172.16.40.15', 'contractor_disgruntled@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Internal Slack & Campus Badge Access', 'Slack DLP Alert: Critical ThreatMatch ''killing me'' ''harm anyone'' ''destroy''. Origin: Campus Building B.', '2026-09-28T17:50:47Z', 'Insider threat driven by contractor disgruntlement and possible mental‑health crisis, leading to hostile statements and intent to cause physical harm.', NULL, 'Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.', 'Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.', '', 'Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.', '2026-09-28T17:50:47Z', '2026-09-28T18:03:02Z', '{"incident_classification": "Physical Safety & Hostile Statement / Threat Alert", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "A contractor posted a Slack message containing explicit threats of killing, harming others, and destroying the office. The language indicates an imminent risk to personnel and facilities, triggering a high\u2011severity safety alert.", "possible_root_cause": "Employee/contractor disgruntlement leading to hostile intent; lack of real\u2011time threat mitigation controls on internal communications.", "indicators": ["Slack DLP alert flagging phrases \"killing me\", \"harm anyone\", \"destroy\"", "Source IP 172.16.40.15 associated with campus badge access system"], "investigation_steps": ["Collect full Slack conversation history for the user", "Extract badge access logs for the past 48\u202fhours", "Verify the contractor''s employment status and recent HR notes", "Interview the user (if safe) or obtain a statement from witnesses", "Preserve all logs and communications as evidence"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately suspend the contractor''s Slack account and revoke all badge access privileges", "Escalate to Physical Security and notify on\u2011site security personnel; consider law\u2011enforcement involvement", "Preserve the Slack message and badge logs for forensic analysis", "Issue a temporary lockdown of the affected building area until the threat is assessed"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Rapid containment prevents the user from physically accessing the site or communicating further threats, protecting staff and assets while evidence is secured for investigation.", "historical_evidence": "Past incidents recorded in Hindsight (e.g., HIST-001 with similarity scores 0.95, 0.87, 0.79) involved identical threat language on internal channels. In each case, immediate account suspension, badge revocation, and escalation to security resulted in safe resolution without injury. Those precedents demonstrate that swift access denial and security notification are effective mitigation steps.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Deploy real\u2011time DLP that auto\u2011quarantines messages containing violent threats and triggers automatic account lockout", "Implement mandatory threat\u2011awareness and de\u2011escalation training for all contractors and employees, with periodic refresher courses"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "95%", "similarity_score": 0.95, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "87%", "similarity_score": 0.87, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}, {"id": "HIST-001", "title": "", "type": "Cyber Threat", "similarity": "79%", "similarity_score": 0.79, "root_cause": "Historical Root Cause", "investigation_process": "Historical Investigation", "actions_taken": "Mitigation applied", "successful_resolution": "Resolved successfully", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "", "post_mortem_information": ""}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hs-INC-2026-1047');
INSERT INTO "M SRI HARI SAI ESWAR" ("id", "title", "type", "severity", "status", "description", "source_ip", "username", "affected_system", "additional_logs", "timestamp", "root_cause", "investigation_process", "actions_taken", "successful_resolution", "analyst_feedback", "lessons_learned", "created_at", "resolved_at", "ai_analysis", "hindsight_memory_id") VALUES ('INC-2026-1048', 'Toxic Workplace Communication & Abusive Harassment', 'Physical Threat & Hostile Statement', 'HIGH', 'RESOLVED', 'User submitted toxic profanity, abusive insults, and threats: ''you idiot bastard, I will ruin you and make you pay''.', '10.0.8.44', 'hostile_employee@sentinelcorp.internal', 'Microsoft Teams #general & Helpdesk', 'Teams DLP Monitor: High-severity Alert: Profanity, targeted toxic harassment, and verbal threats detected.', '2026-09-28T18:03:09Z', 'Insider threat driven by employee disgruntlement and possible personal or mental‑health issues, leading to hostile verbal threats toward colleagues.', NULL, 'Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.', 'Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.', 'AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.', 'Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.', '2026-09-28T18:03:09Z', '2026-09-28T18:03:27Z', '{"incident_classification": "Physical Safety & Hostile Statement / Threat Alert", "severity_assessment": "HIGH", "explanation": "The user posted profanity, personal insults, and an explicit threat (''I will ruin you and make you pay'') via Microsoft Teams, triggering a high\u2011severity DLP alert. The language constitutes a credible threat of harm and violates corporate safety policies, requiring immediate protective action.", "possible_root_cause": "Insider threat driven by employee disgruntlement and possible personal or mental\u2011health issues, leading to hostile verbal threats toward colleagues.", "indicators": ["Profanity and abusive language detected by Teams DLP", "Explicit threat statement ''I will ruin you and make you pay''", "Source IP 10.0.8.44 associated with hostile_employee@sentinelcorp.internal", "Alert on #general and Helpdesk channels"], "investigation_steps": ["Collect full Teams chat transcript and DLP alert details", "Preserve workstation, network, and authentication logs for chain\u2011of\u2011custody", "Cross\u2011reference badge reader logs to confirm physical presence on\u2011site", "Interview witnesses and the alleged perpetrator under HR supervision", "Coordinate with Physical Security, HR, Legal, and possibly law enforcement"], "recommended_response": ["Immediately revoke the employee''s physical access badge and suspend AD/SSO/VPN accounts", "Notify Corporate Physical Security and dispatch on\u2011site security personnel", "Preserve all digital evidence and create a forensic image of the affected workstation", "Escalate to HR and Legal for disciplinary and potential law\u2011enforcement action", "Apply temporary network isolation if further malicious activity is suspected"], "reason_for_recommendation": "Rapid badge revocation and account suspension prevent the individual from accessing facilities or systems while the threat is assessed, protecting personnel safety and limiting potential escalation. Evidence preservation ensures a defensible investigation and supports any legal or HR actions.", "historical_evidence": "Past incidents INC-2026-1047, INC-2026-1045, and INC-2026-1042 involved identical hostile verbal threats. In each case, immediate badge revocation, credential rotation, MFA enforcement, and coordination with Physical Security halted the threat and resulted in zero unauthorized persistence. The successful resolutions documented in those post\u2011mortems justify applying the same containment steps here with high confidence.", "prevention_suggestions": ["Deploy automated DLP integration that triggers real\u2011time badge revocation and account suspension for violent threat detections", "Implement mandatory employee wellness checks and confidential mental\u2011health resources", "Conduct regular workplace\u2011violence awareness training and clear escalation procedures", "Enforce zero\u2011trust network access with continuous monitoring for insider\u2011threat indicators", "Audit and rotate privileged credentials quarterly and require MFA for all privileged accounts"], "similar_historical_incidents": [{"id": "INC-2026-1047", "title": "Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Insider threat driven by contractor disgruntlement and possible mental\u2011health crisis, leading to hostile statements and intent to cause physical harm.", "investigation_process": null, "actions_taken": "Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "analyst_feedback": "", "lessons_learned": "Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1047 - Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''. Root Cause: Insider threat driven by contractor disgruntlement and possible mental\u2011health crisis, leading to hostile statements and intent to cause physical harm.. Resolution: Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected."}, {"id": "INC-2026-1045", "title": "Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Disgruntled contractor with personal grievance leading to insider threat behavior", "investigation_process": null, "actions_taken": "Approved and applied recommended perimeter firewall rules, rotated credentials, and enabled MFA.", "successful_resolution": "Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected.", "analyst_feedback": "AI recommendation approved by SOC Analyst.", "lessons_learned": "Enforce key-only authentication with continuous port exposure monitoring.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1045 - Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''. Root Cause: Disgruntled contractor with personal grievance leading to insider threat behavior. Resolution: Mitigation verified; zero unauthorized persistence detected."}, {"id": "INC-2026-1042", "title": "Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''", "type": "Physical Threat & Hostile Statement", "similarity": "98%", "similarity_score": 0.98, "root_cause": "Insider threat incident involving hostile verbal statements and safety escalation violating corporate safety policies.", "investigation_process": "1. Ingested internal communication telemetry containing violent hostile threat indicators.\n2. Cross-referenced badge reader logs at facility turnstiles to locate individual''s physical presence.\n3. Coordinated immediate priority triage with Corporate Physical Security and HR Legal.\n4. Preserved digital audit trail and workstation activity logs for chain-of-custody documentation.", "actions_taken": "Revoked physical access badges immediately; suspended Active Directory, SSO, and VPN sessions; dispatched physical security personnel for on-site assessment.", "successful_resolution": "Perimeter and facility access secured; employee escorted off premises by security with formal HR and legal protocol initiated.", "analyst_feedback": "kill", "lessons_learned": "Integrate automated workplace violence threat detection with real-time physical badge revocation workflows.", "post_mortem_information": "Post-Mortem: INC-2026-1042 - Threat to Life & Violent Statement Alert: ''he was killing me''. Root Cause: Insider threat incident involving hostile verbal statements and safety escalation violating corporate safety policies.. Resolution: Perimeter and facility access secured; employee escorted off premises by security with formal HR and legal protocol initiated."}], "memory_augmented": true}', 'hs-INC-2026-1048');
